{"title":"2018 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/8/6c816a32bdde966f32fc0ed0aec96453ad0ef8df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 &lt; a_2 &lt; a_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"98\" height=\"12\" /> be three positive integers in the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2c5505caae098da304b7d7f19acb6b60f500d32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[1,14]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/f/07fc1c006a8fab7fafc2b31baa05243a56087730.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2-a_1\\ge3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"92\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/a/efa0228ef74a0cc826c432871df9dc082beeab29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3-a_2\\ge3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"92\" height=\"17\" />. How many diﬀerent choices of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/0/250db015f4a06bd9445a939dfc3aa60667c1a4e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_1,a_2,a_3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" /> exist?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have 14 balls. Place 3. Now we have to fill 4 gaps with 11 balls such that two gaps have atleast 3 balls in them. Place those 6, leaving us with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/1/221b30bdd137fd99db3356f8eeb0d04327ab45c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c+d = 5, a,b,c,d \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"237\" height=\"18\" />, which has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/4/804df644fa8466d8d4a8cdd8a2fb5b3a7545bebb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{10}{3} = 120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"100\" height=\"55\" /> solutions.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II\" title=\"2018 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II\">2018 UNM-PNM Contest II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems\" title=\"2018 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2018 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://mathcontest.unm.edu/\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/i